<title>USA: PVC says Kirkland buys majority stake.</title>
<headline>PVC says Kirkland buys majority stake.</headline>
<dateline>EATONTOWN, N.J. 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>PVC Container Corp said on Monday that Kirtland Capital Partners purchased from Liechtenstein's Rimer Anstalt all of Rimer's equity interest in PVC, or about 63 percent of the outstanding shares of PVC common stock.</p>
<p>The existing management will remain but the company will expand its board of directors to include independent, outside directors, said PVC, which manufactures and distributes plastic containers and compounds.</p>
<p>Kirtland Capital, based in Willoughby Hills, Ohio, is a privately funded investment group.</p>
